; set-spool-size
; Records or corrects the spool mounted on a tool: nominal net weight and what
; is left on it. The same questions the filament load asks at its feed prompt - one call
; to spool/confirm.g without A1, so the tool's current values are preselected:
; a dropdown of the common sizes ("Other..." for a free value in grams), the spool body
; from the spool catalog (macro edit-spool-catalog, gives the empty-spool weight), then the
; weight on a scale - the tare is subtracted automatically. With a material.g the size
; dropdown lists the profile's own spool sizes instead.
; Persisted per tool in sys/generated/spool<tool>.g together with the filament's
; density, which the consumption tracker (spool/track.g) needs. Cancelling the first
; prompt keeps everything. Use it when a spool is swapped without a filament change
; (same material, new spool) or to correct the tracked remaining weight.
; Allowed while a print is paused (a spool change), never while it prints.

if job.file.fileName != null && state.status != "paused"
  echo "Error: a print job is running - abort!"
  M99

; which tool: T<n> when called with it, else asked when a second tool is defined (with
; T0 and T1 in two motion systems DWC's current tool is only that of its own motion
; system), preselected on the current tool
var tool = min(max(state.currentTool, 0), 1)
if exists(param.T)
  set var.tool = (param.T == 1) ? 1 : 0
elif #tools > 1 && tools[1] != null
  M291 R"Spool" P"Record the spool of which tool?" S4 K{"Tool 0","Tool 1"} F{var.tool} J2
  if result != 0             ; J2 leaves input undefined - result must be tested right here
    M99
  set var.tool = input
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/spool/confirm.g" T{var.tool}

M291 R"Spool" P{"Tool " ^ var.tool ^ ": " ^ floor(global.spool_remaining[var.tool]) ^ " g of " ^ global.spool_net_weight[var.tool] ^ " g spool" ^ (global.spool_density[var.tool] > 0 ? "" : " (no density - not tracked)")} S1 T0
M400 ; sbc specific
